```c
table_group->ops->take_ownership(table_group);
```
```c
// Removed set_window() calls
```
```c
// No programming of existing IOMMU tables to hardware
```
Reason:
The removal of the `set_window()` calls in the `tce_iommu_take_ownership_ddw` function meant that when a new group was attached to a container that already had IOMMU tables, the existing tables were not programmed to the hardware. This omission broke the functionality required for VFIO PCI hotplug operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < IOMMU_TABLE_GROUP_MAX_TABLES; ++i) {
    struct iommu_table *tbl = container->tables[i];
    if (!tbl)
        continue;
    ret = table_group->ops->set_window(table_group, i, tbl);
}
```
```c
table_group->ops->release_ownership(table_group);
```
Reason:
The added loop iterates over the existing IOMMU tables and calls `set_window()` for each one, ensuring that the tables are properly programmed to the hardware when a new group is attached. This restores the necessary functionality for VFIO PCI hotplug operations that was lost due to the previous removal of these calls.

